      <h2>The Risk of Cold Outbound WhatsApp Broadcasting</h2>
      <p>Many businesses mistakenly treat WhatsApp like email, purchasing bulk contact databases and sending promotional broadcasts to thousands of phone numbers. In 2026, this approach faces severe roadblocks:</p>
      <ul>
        <li><strong>Skyrocketing Unit Economics:</strong> Sending 10,000 marketing templates can easily cost $300–$800+ per blast depending on the recipient country code.</li>
        <li><strong>Immediate Quality Rating Penalties:</strong> When users tap "Block & Report Spam", Meta drops your phone number's quality score from Green to Red. Continued complaints trigger automatic messaging limits or complete account termination.</li>
        <li><strong>Low Intent & Ignored Alerts:</strong> Unsolicited promotional blasts yield conversion rates under 1.5%, wasting capital on unreceptive audiences.</li>
      </ul>

      <h2>The Inbound Click-to-Chat Advantage</h2>
      <p>The antidote to rising platform costs is the <strong>Inbound Flywheel</strong>. Instead of pushing unwanted messages to cold contacts, you place frictionless click-to-chat access points where prospects are actively looking for solutions.</p>

